 r"I am writing to apply for the Data Analyst position in the RFU's Advanced Data Analytics team. I recently completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have worked on pulling the right data together in SQL and Python, building models and dashboards on top of it, and turning the result into a recommendation someone could act on. I am particularly interested in this role because it starts with insight and dashboards and grows into segmentation, propensity and lifetime value modelling, which is exactly the direction I want my career to take.",

 r"What attracts me most to the RFU is that the analysis has a visible end point: more fans coming back, more players staying in the game, and volunteers who feel supported. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved. The posting describes challenging assumptions so that strategy is informed by data rather than intuition, and that is the part of analytics I want to do.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I mine merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python to find the growth and operations drivers behind the UK marketplace, and I build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that commercial and operations teams use to set targets and track initiatives. Presenting to product, operations and commercial stakeholders is the normal shape of my week, and the recurring lesson has been that the first metric someone asks for is rarely the one that answers their question. I also used Claude Code to build an AI agent that automates repetitive steps of my own analytics workflow, which my team and partner teams now use, so I would be glad to contribute to the team's work on analytics agents.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a medical AI engagement. I designed a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension rubric, which the client adopted as their acceptance standard, and built a Python pipeline calling six LLM APIs that produced and scored over 2,400 responses. I then ran blinded paired A/B tests to measure whether a medically reviewed knowledge graph improved answer quality, and reported which differences the data supported and which it did not. Designing the measure before running the test is the habit I would bring to campaign and A/B test evaluation at the RFU.",

 r"My MSc dissertation applies predictive and causal machine learning to 458,840 UK Biobank participants. I compared a logistic regression baseline with tree-based models, focused on calibration rather than chasing a higher score, and used causal forests to estimate how different groups respond to lifestyle changes. The results are delivered as an interactive Streamlit tool so that non-specialists can explore scenarios without touching the code. That project is the closest thing I have done to a segmentation and propensity suite, and it taught me to check that a model is reliable before anyone acts on it.",

 r"At Ipsos Strategy3 I structured and analysed data from more than 80 healthcare professional interviews, built market-sizing and forecasting models, and turned the analysis into dashboards and recommendations for client stakeholders. That is where I learned to present a finding to an audience who wants the implication rather than the method.",

 r"I should be clear about one gap. I have built dashboards in Power BI and Streamlit rather than Tableau, and I have not yet worked with ticketing or CRM data or with AWS Glue and SageMaker. My SQL, Python and modelling foundations are solid and I have picked up new tooling quickly before, but I would be learning that stack in my first weeks rather than arriving with it.",

 r"I would bring the RFU strong SQL and Python, hands-on experience building predictive models and dashboards, and the habit of checking whether an analysis actually holds up before recommending it. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship. I am based in London and can work from Allianz Stadium as required.",

